<title>USA: Amoco Corp drops India methane project.</title>
<headline>Amoco Corp drops India methane project.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco Corp said Thursday it has decided to scrap a proposed 40 billion cubic meter coalbed methane project in India, due to slow negotiations.</p>
<p>The three phase plan announced in 1994 would have cost about $1 billion, spokesman Jim Spangler said, adding that the company was now looking at projects in Poland and China.</p>
<p>&quot;The progress in the negotiations was not keeping pace with some of the other projects,&quot; Spangler said of the India project.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
